            <ArticleTitle>Dissociation between improvement in angina pectoris and myocardial perfusion after transmyocardial revascularization with an excimer laser.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>229-31, A9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Xenon chloride excimer laser transmyocardial revascularization significantly reduced angina in all patients and increased regional myocardial perfusion in most patients; however, there was no correlation between symptomatic improvement and flow improvement. Patients' symptomatic improvement preceded improved perfusion by several months.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
